            // rdfs:comment "General information: The seaward boundary of the area is a line from the Mull of Kintyre to Coreswall Point on the Galloway peninsula. The area extends to the tidal limit of the estuary of the River Clyde.\n<br> The term \"Clyde Sea Area\" was used by Hugh Robert Mill (1889) who did pioneering oceanographic and meteorological work in this area. <br> <i>Source: </i>Mill, H.R. (1889) The Clyde Sea Area. I. Physical Geography. II. Salinity and chemical composition of the water. Edinburgh Philosophical Transactions, 36: 641-729." ;
